  "honorsAndAwards": [
   {
    "title": "Real Time Animation Course Directors Award",
    "description": "In the Real Time Animator course, students are tasked with writing an FBX animation importer. We were encouraged to get creative and add in anything else related to graphics. \n\nI won this award because I decided to step outside of the box and work with OpenGL ES 2.0 on android. This was uncharted territory to me at the time, I was new to Android Studio, OpenGL, and Java. To push myself even further, I implemented the Google Cardboard API to make the render capable of VR. ",
    "issueDate": {},
    "issuer": "Issued by Jonathan Burnside · Feb 2016"
   },
   {
    "title": "Structure of Game Design Course Director Award",
    "description": "During my Structure of Game Design class, we were tasked with designing and coding an original 2D game with the DirectX 2D API. The game I developed, \"Where's The Beef!?!?\", is about a UFO trying to pick up cows while avoiding missiles from a government agency. \n\nI won this award because I pushed myself heavily to achieve the vision I had for the game. I composed all of the art in the game, creating sprite sheets and trying to achieve a sandpaper look that I was inspired by. I also took the theme and extended it to the Main Menu, as well as the Options and Credits screens. ",
    "issueDate": {},
    "issuer": "Oct 2014"
   }
